WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.370
Joe: A Brit and an American swap countries

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:06.412
to try each other's KFC.
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:10.620
We're going to start with
some things you can get

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.630
in both the US and the UK
to see if there are some

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.797
subtle differences in
taste or anything else.

00:00:14.797 --> 00:00:15.720
The first thing for me to try,

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.280
the main event, the fried chicken.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.750
So, this is just original recipe chicken.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.490
I've got what looks to be a thigh piece.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.850
Visually, I think it probably
looks slightly more appealing

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.350
than British fried chicken
from KFC tends to look.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:32.125
I always struggle to identify

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:34.260
where the bones are in pieces of KFC.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.960
I don't want to just bite
straight into a bone.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.220
Mm-hmm.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.050
OK, yeah, this is good.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.550
Compared to the UK, I think I definitely

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:42.800
am getting more flavor.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.550
I think a fair amount of that
is coming from the breading.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.596
It's actual seasoning and flavor.

00:00:47.596 --> 00:00:49.950
It's a thick, juicy piece of chicken.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.385
I don't want to go back to eating regular

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:52.920
British KFC after this.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.690
Right, this six-piece bucket.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.950
This looks like it has more skin

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.390
than what we got in the
restaurant, I will say.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.748
So already this looks like
it has a better batter to it.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.730
That is so bland.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.950
I can taste the flavor.
It's just not as strong,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.750
and I'm assuming that's the chemicals

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.360
we put in our food to
make it taste like, wah!

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.620
The next thing that we
wanted to compare was

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.660
popcorn chicken, which I
think in the UK is a pretty

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.520
iconic menu item, although weirdly enough

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.010
they've actually cut it from
the menu in the US right now,

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:17.880
the exception being that

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.800
they will still add it to famous bowls.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:20.760
But we'll get to that later.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.470
So I guess for the time being I will try

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.750
a US chicken nugget and
see how that compares.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.750
I mean, this just kind of
looks like popcorn chicken.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.620
Definitely a bit more dry on the palate.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.380
Again, I don't see why they've
gotten rid of popcorn chicken

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.240
in lieu of these, because
popcorn chicken is

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.740
effectively the same thing.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:38.860
That's like a shot!

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.836
[air horn blowing]

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:41.794
Oh, half in.

00:01:41.794 --> 00:01:43.202
No. I don't taste anything.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.930
So far I would say that KFC chicken,

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.810
both on the bone and popcorn,

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.330
in the US, the flavor is more pronounced

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:54.390
and has more of, like,
a savory flavor to it.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.563
This flavor has training wheels.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.547
It'll get there someday!

00:02:00.642 --> 00:02:01.890
Firstly, there are some twists

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.320
on the classic fried chicken
which we can't usually find.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:07.980
The first variety we have here
is the spicy fried chicken.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.440
I mean, visually this looks fairly similar

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.810
to just the sort of
standard original recipe.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.930
Although I will say the
breading looks pretty good.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.300
You get a lot of these
little flakes of breading,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:20.853
which really tend to get
crisp and stay crisp.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.090
I don't know if there's
enough to call it spicy,

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.563
because I'm not a guy who has
a super-high spice tolerance,

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:29.942
and for me that's, like, warm,
but not much more than that.

00:02:29.942 --> 00:02:31.260
But it's very pleasant, and I do think

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.060
it's crispier than the original recipe.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.530
Very juicy, flavorful.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.460
I think this is really good.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.307
I think I would be tempted to buy

00:02:37.307 --> 00:02:39.630
this over just classic original recipe.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.640
And it's not just spicy chicken
that's available in the US.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.933
You can also get another
type called extra crispy.

00:02:43.933 --> 00:02:45.750
As the name suggests, it's
the regular fried chicken,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.040
but made extra crispy.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.070
I think extra crispy
should be the KFC chicken,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.010
and then the original
should be, like, diet.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.673
For some reason, the branch
that we went to today

00:02:54.673 --> 00:02:56.515
didn't have it in the form of regular,

00:02:56.515 --> 00:02:57.889
original recipe chicken,

00:02:57.889 --> 00:03:00.480
but they did have it in the
form of a chicken little.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.160
I'm just going to break off the end bit

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.552
that was untouched by the mayo

00:03:03.552 --> 00:03:05.410
to see if it is actually crispy or not.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.950
I don't think this is extra crispy.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.720
Even though they told us it was.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.737
Maybe their crispinator was
broken today or something.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.070
KFC US is very good at
cooking chicken on the bone,

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.380
less good when it comes to
cooking chicken off the bone,

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.180
because this is a little
bit dry, a little bit chewy.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.558
Moving on, the snack wrap.
This one is the flamin' hot.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.377
Oh, wow. This has got some heat to it!

00:03:29.377 --> 00:03:30.780
OK, UK!

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.940
Yeah, that's, I like
this. This is really good.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:34.714
Kansas barbecue. OK.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:37.470
This barbecue sauce is pretty good.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.090
I mean, this is definitely
a sweeter sauce,

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:42.330
which I think is indicative
of Kansas City barbecue.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.350
Anyway, yeah, not bad.

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.932
Sweet chili bites.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.786
Too sweet. Not that spicy.

00:03:48.786 --> 00:03:50.640
Now we're on to an item
which I've been watching from

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.430
across the pond with a mixture
of horror and fascination.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.650
It's the KFC famous bowl.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.820
Instead of me trying to explain it,

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.230
I feel like we should
just get Joe in here.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.180
Joe, do you want to come and
explain the famous bowl to me?

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.595
A little bit of everything
that's on the menu,

00:04:01.595 --> 00:04:03.360
just in bowl form,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.508
for anyone who just pretty
much has given up on life

00:04:05.508 --> 00:04:08.040
and doesn't care as long as
they get it in the stomach.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:09.090
Thanks, Joe.
Joe: You're welcome.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.177
Harry: It's looking more like
an infamous bowl right now.

00:04:11.177 --> 00:04:12.235
I'm going to ...

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:15.840
It's not horrible.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.400
There's just a lot going on.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.200
There's a lot of flavors fighting

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.960
with each other right
now, vying for supremacy.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.660
The main thing I get I
think is the corn, actually.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.615
I would've assumed that
the mash and the chicken

00:04:26.615 --> 00:04:28.650
would've been kind of
the stars of the show.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.507
But if anything, it's
everything else in there

00:04:30.507 --> 00:04:32.640
that you can actually taste more.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:34.080
To me, it feels a little bit

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.450
like you're eating baby food for adults.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.310
I was going to say I'm more
excited to try the next bowl,

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.990
but I don't know if excited is the word.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:42.180
Maybe less anxious to try the next bowl.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.910
This is the KFC mac 'n' cheese bowl,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:48.869
but the kind of color on that
is some cause for concern.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.483
So, I think this actually works
in harmony with the chicken

00:04:54.483 --> 00:04:56.100
much better than the famous bowl does.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.380
If I had to get a bowl, I
think I would be leaning more

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:00.660
towards the mac 'n' cheese
bowl than the famous bowl.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.820
Next up is the KFC pot pie.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:05.460
It's funny to see this on
the menu at a KFC in the US

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.185
because I feel like meat pies

00:05:07.185 --> 00:05:09.360
are generally associated
with Britain more.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.901
We love a meat pie in the UK.

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:13.484
Steak pie, chicken pie,

00:05:13.484 --> 00:05:15.870
Greggs, Pukka Pies, all that good stuff.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.760
So, with a meat pie in the
UK, what you'll often get

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.410
is the pastry on the bottom as well.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.270
So it's like a self-contained pie.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:23.340
Whereas I think with a pot
pie, you just have a layer

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.020
of pastry on top and
then filling underneath,

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.520
and there's no bottom layer of crust.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.519
But let's find out.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.360
They haven't skimped on the carrot.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.730
I taste a lot of the carrot flavor.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.512
In the UK, for example, with
a meat pie you tend to get

00:05:34.512 --> 00:05:37.170
a gravy that will kind of
run out when you cut into it.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.750
But this is staying on the spoon.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.520
It's not running off the spoon.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.670
It's not great, but it's not bad either.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.220
It's like, the sauce needs
a little bit more seasoning,

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.420
I think. It's a little bit bland.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.280
Bit more salt and pepper
would not go amiss there.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.840
I think with a few minor adjustments,

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.160
they could make this really good,

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.750
and I do think Brits would go for this.

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:56.694
This is super weird. Look at that!

00:05:56.694 --> 00:05:57.654
There's a hash brown in there.

00:05:57.654 --> 00:05:59.160
What does that have to do with tower?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.183
Not much.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:03.683
Hm.

00:06:03.683 --> 00:06:06.300
I like everything that this is made of.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.452
Together, I don't think it works.

00:06:08.452 --> 00:06:10.707
If I was to get this, I'd
ask them to separate it

00:06:10.707 --> 00:06:12.660
across three containers

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.240
and just eat the hash
brown, then the chicken,

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:16.800
finish it off with a slice of cheese.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:17.760
There you go.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.390
This would be closer to
what our extra crispy is.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:22.650
So this is supposed to be the spicy one.

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:24.292
It's going to zing me with spice?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:30.720
Not bad.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.870
It's not that I dislike
anything I've had so far,

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.730
it's that it's all 60%
to 70% as far as flavor

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:41.910
and intensity that I'm used
to in the United States.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.580
You can also get yourself a zinger stacker

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.170
and a zinger tower burger.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.820
Yo, this is a thick one.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:48.900
Wow!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:52.290
I'm not going to bite into
this, but, man, that's a lot.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:55.260
This would be right at
home on the US menu.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:57.072
This would be like, "Yes, of course."

00:06:57.072 --> 00:06:58.350
It'd be, like, the double
zinger, and everyone's like,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.690
"Yeah, of course it's double."

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.890
OK.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.720
Vegan burger.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.760
It kind of looks like chicken.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.890
The mayo pretty much missed it, right?

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:08.910
See how it came?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.510
So I gotta kind of activate the mayo.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.445
Twist your vegan sandwich
before you eat it!

00:07:15.445 --> 00:07:17.420
Should I even ask what the mayo's made of?

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.690
I mean, when you rip it apart, it's like

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.180
one of those big erasers that
you get when you're a kid.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:26.250
I mean, I wouldn't just
want to eat this in general,

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.820
but as far as a fake
meat, it's pretty close.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.170
And I don't know why if you were vegan

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:34.590
you'd be like, "Finally, a
chicken sandwich at KFC."

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:35.970
No, you can eat this, there's
no chicken meat in it.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:36.930
It's like, yeah, but you're still

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.610
killing them by the millions.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:39.990
So, there is a category in the menu

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.240
of twisters, rice boxes, and salads.

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:44.730
They had no rice boxes or salads.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.554
They did, however, have the twisters.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:50.707
But this is called a twister, not a wrap.

00:07:50.707 --> 00:07:51.900
Leon: It's twisted.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:52.868
What's twisted about it?

00:07:52.868 --> 00:07:53.701
Well, it's not twisted.

00:07:53.701 --> 00:07:56.100
It looks like they took a chicken
breast and cut it in half.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.233
And this was, like, one long tender.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.630
I mean, it's also smaller.

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:04.388
I bet they wanted to appeal
to a more male demographic.

00:08:04.388 --> 00:08:06.300
So, "Don't get a wrap, get a twister!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.980
I'm a big man! I don't want a wrap.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.200
I want a twister! Yeah, it's twisted!

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.220
Wraps are for the ladies,

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.800
but the dudes have twisters. Ah!"

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.450
I don't think that, they think that.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.830
KFC, shame on you.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.293
Let's talk about some exclusive sides

00:08:18.293 --> 00:08:19.710
that you can't find in the UK.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:21.270
Firstly, if the mac 'n' cheese bowl is

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:22.830
too much mac 'n' cheese for you,

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.930
you can just get a little cup as a side.

00:08:24.930 --> 00:08:27.180
You can also get a side of corn.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:28.920
You guys just produce so much of it.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.450
You can't get rid of it fast enough.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.720
I'm not trying corn on the cob.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:38.670
Here in the UK, you guys
have corn on the cob.

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:41.760
Obviously ours is corn off the
cob, but this would be easier

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.010
for driving or eating on the go, right?

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.510
Have you ever seen someone
walking down the street

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.398
just chewing on a cob on a stick?

00:08:47.398 --> 00:08:48.720
It's on a stick!

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.800
You've never seen that?

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:52.050
Keep your eyes peeled. I would
like to get that trend going.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.490
And, of course, apparently it wouldn't be

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:56.040
a US fast-food menu without biscuits.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.720
This is an American biscuit.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.310
It looks a lot like a British scone,

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.390
at least on the outside.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.000
However, generally I think
it's a bit more bready

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:05.337
and maybe slightly drier than a scone.

00:09:05.337 --> 00:09:06.690
[thudding]

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:07.683
Texture check.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.590
It's confusing because
with a British scone,

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:12.436
they're generally sweetened with sugar

00:09:12.436 --> 00:09:14.295
because they're eaten with
things like jam and cream,

00:09:14.295 --> 00:09:16.830
and it's more of an afternoon
tea/dessert type thing,

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:18.270
whereas these ones are
supposed to be eaten

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:21.330
with a savory meal but
actually smell kind of sweet.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.740
I think of the biscuits I've tried

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.110
from fast-food menus in the US so far,

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:26.340
this is probably my favorite one,

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.540
but it's somewhere between, like,

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.850
a British scone and a bread roll.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:30.780
Baked beans.

00:09:32.072 --> 00:09:35.478
Ugh. Eh. Yeah, these
are way more tomatoey.

00:09:35.478 --> 00:09:36.900
To-MAH-to-ey, excuse me.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.073
The tomato sauce that
it's in is similar to

00:09:39.073 --> 00:09:40.920
whatever Spaghettios come in.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:42.540
I will never be in the mood for that.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.503
Southern rice.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.390
What the hell?

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.340
I don't know what they think Southern is.

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.960
I'm surprised at how different it is.

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.953
You'd think an international food chain

00:09:50.953 --> 00:09:52.038
would want it to be the same everywhere,

00:09:52.038 --> 00:09:54.540
but playing to the UK tastes, I assume.

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:56.640
KFC in the US has a bunch of sauce options

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.130
that we can't get in the UK,
which means it's time for:

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:01.620
Sauce talk, "Foreign Exchange"!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.390
The theme seems to be that
they have a lot of honey

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:05.940
on the menu when it comes to
their sauces at KFC in the US.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.160
The sauces on offer here are hot sauce,

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:10.963
honey sauce, a honey barbecue sauce,

00:10:10.963 --> 00:10:14.430
KFC sauce, and yet more
honey, a honey mustard.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.493
I usually like a honey
mustard, but I do think

00:10:16.493 --> 00:10:19.390
you have to get the balance
of honey and mustard right.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:22.190
Yeah, that's not bad. That's
a pretty well-balanced

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:25.023
honey mustard, I think.
I'm intrigued by KFC sauce.

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.570
I quite like it.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:28.980
I really can't put my finger on exactly

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:29.910
what's in it right now.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.485
Next up we've got the honey barbecue.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:36.210
Oh, extremely sweet.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.670
Both on the honey side and
even on the barbecue side.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.990
Let's have a look at the honey sauce.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.156
It's fine. It does taste
pretty much just like honey.

00:10:42.156 --> 00:10:44.093
And then finally they have a hot sauce.

00:10:44.093 --> 00:10:46.110
Yeah, that's pretty comparable
to, like, a Frank's RedHot.

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.235
Barbecue!

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:49.740
OK, Kentucky smoked barbecue.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:50.940
Actually, this is on point.

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.130
Sticky sweet chili sauce.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:54.317
Why is it sticky?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:56.910
Yeah! Oh, that's good.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.920
All right, garlic buttermilk mayo.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.002
I like all three of
those things separately.

00:11:02.394 --> 00:11:04.060
Mm! Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.637
Now let's look at some exclusive drinks

00:11:05.637 --> 00:11:08.670
served in these delightful
"Diablo"-branded cups.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:11.370
You guys love a advertisement
tie-in, don't you?

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:14.850
So, I believe this one is Starry,
Joe's beloved Sierra Mist,

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:18.300
unfortunately culled recently
and replaced by Starry.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.040
Let's give it a try.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.510
It's more what I'm used to, I guess,

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:24.630
from a UK version of a
lemonade-style drink.

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:27.655
And, of course, we have
a US-style lemonade.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.485
It's pretty good. Again,
to me it's slightly weird

00:11:31.485 --> 00:11:32.976
what Americans consider lemonade,

00:11:32.976 --> 00:11:34.560
considering coming from the UK,

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:36.090
lemonade is basically Sprite.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.610
It's a clear, carbonated, lemony beverage.

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:39.443
It's pretty good.

00:11:39.443 --> 00:11:42.180
It's probably slightly more
refreshing and hydrating

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.770
than a Sprite is in the UK.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:45.210
There are a couple of
other exclusive drinks

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:46.080
which we can normally get,

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.295
but unfortunately our
local branch did not have,

00:11:48.295 --> 00:11:49.980
devastatingly, because I really wanted

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.380
to try the Mountain Dew Sweet Lightning

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.270
and regular American Mountain Dew.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.287
When we ordered the bottles
of drinks, didn't we think

00:11:56.287 --> 00:11:59.187
it was just going to be, like,
a personal one? I don't know.

00:11:59.187 --> 00:12:00.908
Tango, orange.

00:12:00.908 --> 00:12:02.508
Ugh, 7Up free.

00:12:02.508 --> 00:12:03.722
Pepsi Max cherry.

00:12:03.722 --> 00:12:06.396
Krushems! UK of course has
exclusive Krushem drinks.

00:12:06.396 --> 00:12:08.095
I have them in front of me. I
said, "Give me one of each,"

00:12:08.095 --> 00:12:10.530
and they did. Milkybar.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.363
Mm!

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:12.837
Aero. Is that normal?

00:12:12.837 --> 00:12:16.084
Charlie: It kind of was advertised
as a "healthy" chocolate.

00:12:16.084 --> 00:12:19.332
Leon: Because it's got more
air in there. It's healthy.

00:12:19.332 --> 00:12:20.565
We're still charging the same,

00:12:20.565 --> 00:12:22.830
but you get less in there, so, OK.

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.770
Less calories by default
because it's filled with air.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.240
I might be the last
person to point this out,

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.290
but, like, they took the candy bar,

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:31.110
and they crushed it, and
that's why it's Krushems. OK.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:33.150
Oreo one. I mean, come on.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.340
That's really good. I
would definitely get this.

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:36.173
Dessert.

00:12:36.173 --> 00:12:38.631
Exclusive desserts. You get a
white chocolate chip cookie.

00:12:38.631 --> 00:12:40.530
You can also get a pineapple stick,

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.450
but they didn't have any
at the location we went to.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:45.210
Also, I don't know what
a pineapple stick is.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:47.252
Leon: It's a terrible dessert.
Joe: Why is that dessert?

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.690
I think if I could pick
one item from this menu

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.642
to take back with me to the UK

00:12:53.642 --> 00:12:54.870
and put on our menu over there,

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:56.850
I think it would probably
be the spicy chicken.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.470
I just like how it was
slightly more crispy

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.780
than the regular chicken and
just added a bit more flavor.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.340
The level of heat was really good.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.690
Yeah, I think that
would come back with me.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:06.690
If I could remove one thing
from the US and all other menus

00:13:06.690 --> 00:13:09.390
from KFC, I think it
would be the famous bowl.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.800
I'm sorry, guys. I don't want to start

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.720
some kind of revolutionary war again,

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.880
but I just feel like it's not very good,

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:17.370
because those ingredients
don't really go together,

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:19.110
texturally, it's a bit of a nightmare,

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.550
and honestly there's
just way better things

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.290
you can do with the stuff on the menu.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:25.680
I was really impressed
with the flamin' hot wrap.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:26.850
I might have dogged on
it a little bit earlier

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:29.010
because it was smaller,
but that spicy sauce

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:30.600
you guys have is actually pretty good.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.880
Honorable mention, the vegan burger.

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.630
Obviously, I'm not vegan,
but I guess I was surprised

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.180
by how kind of decent it was.

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.345
It's not my favorite, but, I mean,

00:13:40.345 --> 00:13:43.553
points for it being edible. Way to go.

00:13:43.553 --> 00:13:45.120
I will do everyone a favor,

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.400
and I will say I'm not
cutting a menu item.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:51.060
Let's get that potato
off of your sandwiches.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.996
They just don't work together, period.

00:13:52.996 --> 00:13:54.527
Full activity.

